**2. Register in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Add Problem Details and the custom handler
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<GlobalExceptionHandler>();

var app = builder.Build();

// Must be early in the pipeline
app.UseExceptionHandler();

// Your endpoints - no try-catch needed
app.MapGet("/items/{id}", (int id) =>
{
    if (id < 0) throw new ArgumentException("ID must be positive.");
    if (id == 0) throw new KeyNotFoundException("Item not found.");
    return Results.Ok(new { Id = id, Name = "Example" });
});

app.Run();
```

**How it works:**

- `IExceptionHandler` (available since .NET 8) intercepts all unhandled exceptions globally
- The switch expression maps exception types → HTTP status codes
- For 500s, the actual exception message is hidden; only a generic detail is returned
- `AddProblemDetails()` ensures the response `Content-Type` is `application/problem+json`
- No try-catch needed in individual endpoints

**Example 404 response:**
```json
{
  "status": 404,
  "title": "Not Found",
  "detail": "Item not found."
}
```
